  "body": "Follow-up of #1997. The maintainer asked in chat on 2026-11-15:\n\n\"The Orbit control has changed - It is not rotating around where the mouse pointer is clicking anymore... is that intentional? which issue introduced that?\"\n\nThe work on #1997 found that no commit removed a pointer pivot. The orbit always turned about `Camera::target` (`crates/ui/src/viewport.rs`, `Camera::orbit`). The pointer pivot is a new feature.\n\nWhat to do:\n\n- At the press of an orbit drag, pick the model point under the pointer (`Camera::ray_through` and the pick law in `crates/ui/src/interact.rs`).\n- Turn the view about that point. The point keeps its screen position during the drag.\n- If the press is on empty space, turn about `Camera::target`.\n- Keep `Camera::target` consistent for pan, zoom (`dolly_cursor`) and `frame`.\n- The same rule applies in perspective and orthographic projection.\n- Ephemeral view state only: no command, not saved.\n\nDone means:\n\n- A test pins that the picked point keeps its screen position during an orbit drag, in each projection.\n- A test pins the fallback for a press on empty space.\n- The choice (pivot on the picked point, or on the target moved to the picked point) is recorded in `docs/decisions/`.\n",
